metalive wrote:
>
> What is "vanilla" Nethack?

Vanilla is an Internet-standard term meaning
the good regular unmodified version of anything.
For something to be vanilla it must be good, so
operating systems that used punch cards were never
vanilla.  Vanilla is not a nethack-only term.

Thus vanilla nethack is the latest general
release nethack without added patches, without
custom levels, and so on.

I don't know if vanilla nethack means with or
without tiles.  I use it without tiles but tiles
have been standard for so long many could consider
them vanilla now.

Vanilla is the most popular form of ice cream in
the US and it is also the simplist.  If unflavored
ice cream became the most popular, the term would
become "unflavored" rather than "vanilla".


